154439926, 0.006324432790279388, -0.015435687266290188, -0.030718673020601273, -0.0063117071986198425, 0.009995657950639725, -0.006648925598710775, -0.013017896562814713, 0.021492891013622284, -0.016453705728054047, 0.012407085858285427, 0.03443443402647972, 0.028351781889796257]], "input": ["# SENPE and Pediatric Nutrition Community\n\nThe community is centered around SENPE (Sociedad Española de Nutrición Clínica y Metabolismo) and its collaborations with various organizations and individuals focused on clinical and pediatric nutrition in Spain. Key entities include researchers and associations that contribute to the development of guidelines and best practices in nutrition, particularly for pediatric patients and critically ill individuals.\n\n## SENPE's central role in clinical nutrition\n\nSENPE is a pivotal organization in the field of clinical nutrition in Spain, focusing on hospital malnutrition and providing essential guidelines for nutritional support. Its collaborations with other organizations, such as SEMICYUC and SECP, enhance its influence in developing comprehensive nutritional strategies for critically ill patients. SENPE's commitment to improving nutritional practices is evident through its extensive documentation and management strategies, which are crucial for healthcare professionals in Spain. [Data: Entities (1); Relationships (50, 74, 66)]\n\n## Collaboration with pediatric nutrition specialists\n\nSENPE collaborates closely with ANECIPN, SEGHNP, and SECP to establish and promote standards for pediatric enteral nutrition. This collaboration is vital for ensuring that pediatric patients receive optimal nutritional care, as these organizations work together to create consensus documents and guidelines that address the specific needs of children. The joint efforts of these entities significantly enhance the quality of pediatric nutrition practices in Spain. [Data: Entities (2507, 2506, 2508); Relationships (59, 60, 58)]\n\n## Research contribution